## #02 — PSI-01: bind resolutions before using them
A well-formed hash is not a known return revision. Match a review to an observed
source/revision within the declared target lineage before it can alter a finding
or count as a reviewed pass. Unknown hashes, invalid legacy bindings and invalid
review records remain visible as attention/conflict evidence; retain the last
valid finding state. Do not drop their text, silently close the finding, or invent
a pass. Preserve existing legacy whole-file review support when evidence exists.
Keep finding identity scoped to the appropriate return/source lineage rather
than collapsing unrelated page-local IDs. Explain how exact review_sources bind
to their targets; never infer a target or approval from the disposition prose.

## #03 — PSI-02: causal order and visible conflicts
Use commit ancestry for updates on the same source/lineage, not commit timestamp.
Prime reproduced descendant B unresolved losing to ancestor A verified-fixed
because B's timestamp was older. This must stay unresolved with worktree off.
If two sources/branches contain incompatible incomparable resolutions, expose
both as conflict/attention; no timestamp, registry-order or lexical winner.
Define uncommitted review observations explicitly. A draft observation cannot
silently conceal a conflicting committed open finding. Same-content copies and
repeated observations do not manufacture extra passes. Preserve honest history
incomplete/unknown reporting and read-only operation.

