PSI-01 (bind before use): CORRECTED.
- A review counts only when its hash is a known revision of its declared target. A page Review targets its own page. A review source must name `reviewed_return_path:`, and it must be a registered return of the same lane.
- A legacy whole-file hash binds only when it equals an observed version of that page.
- Unknown hashes, invalid legacy hashes, invalid targets and unbound findings become `invalid-review` attention, with source, hash and finding text kept. They change no finding and count no pass. The last valid state stays.
- Finding identity is `<target path>#<ID>`.
- Prime's case: PS-X unresolved, then a review naming aaaa… with verified-fixed. Before: closed, passes 2, no attention. After: unresolved, open, passes 1, with the aaaa… item visible, worktree on and off.
- Also covered: invalid legacy; review-source target required, unregistered or absent; the same ID on two pages kept as two findings.
- The real 0504/05.05 legacy binding still works (demo A).

PSI-02 (causal order): CORRECTED.
- Committed records for a finding are ordered only by `git merge-base --is-ancestor`, never by date. The frontier decides the state.
- Incomparable resolutions are `conflict`, with every frontier record listed and an attention item. There is no timestamp, registry or lexical winner.
- `git log --topo-order` orders supersedes.
- An uncommitted worktree file identical to HEAD is the same observation. A differing one is a `draft`, reported beside the committed state, never replacing it. A differing draft is a "draft differs from committed" conflict item.
- Passes count distinct bound revisions only.
- Prime's case: A (2030) verified-fixed, then descendant B (2029) unresolved, worktree off. Before: closed. After: unresolved, open.
- Also covered: local behind remote (resolved by ancestry); divergent branches (conflict, both shown); worktree draft versus committed; repeated observations (passes 1); ack-store deletion (unchanged).

Original-test changes, minimal: scoped-key lookups in tests 07, 08 and 08b, and test 11's unbound list, where the identical worktree is now listed once. The before tests are preserved.
